
{0 TIFF}

{! Tiff} is a library for working with TIFF
(Tagged Image File Format) images in OCaml.

It provides functionality for reading and writing
TIFF images and accessing image metadata.

{1 Getting started}

- {{:https://github.com/geocaml/ocaml-tiff#readme}README}
  — Introduction and installation instructions.
- {{:https://github.com/geocaml/ocaml-tiff/tree/main/examples}Examples}
  — Example programs demonstrating library usage.
- {{:https://github.com/geocaml/ocaml-tiff/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md}Contributing}
  — How to build, test and contribute.

{1 Library [tiff]}

The library provides APIs for working with TIFF
images and their associated metadata.

- {!module:Tiff} — Main interface for working
  with TIFF files.
- {!module:Tiff.Ifd} — Access TIFF Image File
  Directory (IFD) metadata.

{2 File access}

The file access types describe how TIFF data
is read from and written to files.

- {!type:Tiff.File.ro} — Read-only file access.
- {!type:Tiff.File.wo} — Write-only file access.
